# Authentication Architecture

Splash

↓

Load Tokens

↓

No Tokens?

↓

Auth Stack

Welcome → Register or Login

↓

Save Tokens

↓

Set Current User (memory)

↓

Home Stack

---

Tokens Exist

↓

Validate Session (`GET /users/me`)

↓

Home Stack

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  Splash[index splash gate] --> LoadTokens[Load tokens]
  LoadTokens -->|none| AuthStack[Auth Stack]
  LoadTokens -->|present| Validate["GET /users/me"]
  Validate -->|ok| HomeStack[Home Tabs]
  Validate -->|401/fail| ClearTokens[deleteTokens] --> AuthStack
  AuthStack --> Welcome
  Welcome --> Login
  Welcome --> Signup
  Login -->|saveTokens + setUser| HomeStack
  Signup -->|saveTokens + setUser| HomeStack
```

## Notes

- User profile is **in-memory only** (AuthContext). Cold start with tokens always revalidates via `/users/me`.
- Tokens live in secure token-storage (`saveTokens` / `deleteTokens`).
- Do not implement axios refresh-token retry until explicitly added.
- Set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` for the API host (Android emulator often `http://10.0.2.2:8080`).
